==Synopsis==
===Prelude===
{{see also|Elseworlds (Arrowverse)#Plot}}

To prepare for the coming crisis, the [[Monitor (Arrowverse)|Monitor]] recruits [[Oliver Queen (Arrowverse)|Oliver Queen]] and [[Martian Manhunter]] and sends the former on missions to collect a variety of items,<ref name="ArrowFinale" /> while he retrieves the body of [[Lex Luthor (Arrowverse)|Lex Luthor]] and revives him.<ref name="SupergirlFinale" /><ref name="Batwoman108Supergirl508" /> Meanwhile, [[Barry Allen (Arrowverse)|Barry Allen]] and [[Iris West-Allen (Arrowverse)|Iris West-Allen]] learn that the crisis date has moved up to December 2019 and that the Flash must die to save billions of lives.<ref name="Flash601" /> Barry travels to [[Earth-3 (Arrowverse)|Earth-3]] to see [[Jay Garrick (Arrowverse)|Jay Garrick]] and [[Joan Williams (Arrowverse)|Joan Williams]], who have been tracking antimatter signatures across the multiverse, to learn more about what happens to him. They send Barry's mind forward in time, making him see billions of timelines where the multiverse is destroyed and one where he dies saving it.<ref name="Flash602" />

While on a mission, Oliver witnesses the destruction of [[Earth-2 (Arrowverse)|Earth-2]] from an antimatter wave.<ref name="Earth2Destroyed" /> In [[Star City (Arrowverse)|Star City]], [[William Clayton (Arrowverse)|William Clayton]], [[Connor Hawke (Arrowverse Earth-1)|Connor Hawke]], and [[Mia Smoak]] time-travel from 2040 to the present,<ref name="Arrow803" /> while Oliver and [[John Diggle (Arrowverse)|John Diggle]] learn that [[Lyla Michaels (Arrowverse)|Lyla Michaels]] has been working with the Monitor.<ref name="Arrow805" /> Moments before the crisis begins, [[Nash Wells]] is pulled into a chamber under [[Central City (Arrowverse)|Central City]] after he is promised a new life.<ref name="Batwoman108Supergirl508" /> As the crisis starts, the sky over [[Central City (DC Comics)|Central City]] and [[Lian Yu (Arrowverse location)|Lian Yu]] turns red. Lyla, now a "harbinger of things to come", collects Oliver and Mia on Lian Yu.<ref name="Flash608" /><ref name="Arrow807" />

On an unspecified Earth, the sky also turns red over Freeland and adversely reacts to [[Jennifer Pierce (Arrowverse)|Jennifer Pierce]]'s powers, tearing her between her Earth and those of two of her doppelgängers. As the Pierce family and [[Peter Gambi (Arrowverse)|Peter Gambi]] try to bring her back, the antimatter wave overtakes them while [[Jefferson Pierce (Arrowverse)|Jefferson Pierce]] is transported away.<ref name="Black Lightning Crisis ep">{{Cite episode |title=The Book of Resistance: Chapter Four: Earth Crisis |episode-link=The Book of Resistance: Chapter Four: Earth Crisis |series=Black Lightning |series-link=Black Lightning (TV series) |network=[[The CW]] |date=December 9, 2019 |season=3 |number=9}}</ref>

===Plot===
Having already destroyed countless parallel universes,{{efn|Those named on-screen include [[Earth-89 (Arrowverse)|Earth-89]], [[Earth-9 (Arrowverse)|Earth-9]], [[Earth-X (Arrowverse)|Earth-X]], and [[Earth-66 (Arrowverse)|Earth-66]].<ref name="CinemaBlendSupergirlCameos" />}} the antimatter wave makes its way to [[Earth-38 (Arrowverse)|Earth-38]]. [[Brainiac 5 (Arrowverse)|Brainiac 5]] detects the wave approaching [[Argo City (Arrowverse)|Argo City]], prompting [[Kara Danvers (Arrowverse)|Kara Danvers]] to warn her mother [[Alura Zor-El (Arrowverse)|Alura Zor-El]], her cousin [[Clark Kent (Arrowverse)|Clark Kent]], and his wife [[Lois Lane (Arrowverse)|Lois Lane]]. Clark and Lois send their son, [[Jonathan Kent (Arrowverse)|Jonathan]], off in an escape pod just before the wave hits. Harbinger brings Oliver, Mia, Barry, [[Kate Kane (Arrowverse)|Kate Kane]], [[Sara Lance]], and [[Ray Palmer (Arrowverse)|Ray Palmer]] to Earth-38 and rescues the Kents from Argo. As Harbinger briefs the heroes on the situation, the Monitor raises a tower to impede the wave while the [[Department of Extranormal Operations (Arrowverse)|DEO]] and [[Lena Luthor (Arrowverse)|Lena Luthor]] evacuate Earth-38's inhabitants. Brainy finds Jonathan's pod on [[Earth-16 (Arrowverse)|Earth-16]], so he, Lois, and Sara leave to retrieve him while the others fight the [[Anti-Monitor (Arrowverse)|Anti-Monitor]]'s forces. Preparing to die, Oliver passes the Green Arrow mantle to Mia. When he learns that Barry is fated to die, however, he argues with the Monitor about their deal.{{efn|As depicted in the 2018 crossover, "[[Elseworlds (Arrowverse)|Elseworlds]]".}} The heroes fight an army of Shadow Demons until the Monitor breaches them off-world. Refusing to leave, Oliver nullifies the Monitor and stays behind to protect the exodus. Lois' team returns to [[Earth-1 (Arrowverse)|Earth-1]] with Jonathan just as the Monitor brings a dying Oliver to say goodbye. Nash, now a "[[Pariah (character)|Pariah]]" for releasing the Anti-Monitor, announces that events have changed and all is lost.<ref name="Crisis Part 1 ep">{{Cite episode |title=Crisis on Infinite Earths: Part One |series=Supergirl |series-link=Supergirl (TV series) |network=[[The CW]] |date=December 8, 2019 |season=5 |number=9}}</ref>

Harbinger recruits [[Earth-74 (Arrowverse)|Earth-74]]'s [[Mick Rory (Arrowverse)|Mick Rory]] so the heroes can use his ''Waverider'' as their headquarters. Following Oliver's death, the Monitor consults the Book of Destiny and learns about four of seven Paragons: Hope (Kara); Destiny (Sara); Truth (a Superman who has suffered "more than any mortal man"); and Courage (the "Bat of the Future"). Clark, Lois, and Iris locate the second Superman on [[Earth-96 (Arrowverse)|Earth-96]], where Lex uses the Book of Destiny to brainwash that Earth's Clark until Lois knocks Lex out. Kara and Kate travel to [[Earth-99 (Arrowverse)|Earth-99]], but fail to recruit its Batman after discovering he murdered his world's Superman while Sara, Barry, Mia, and [[John Constantine (Arrowverse)|John Constantine]] take Oliver to a Lazarus Pit on [[Earth-18 (Arrowverse)|Earth-18]] in an attempt to resurrect him, only to learn his soul is missing. On the ''Waverider'', the Monitor has Ray build a "Paragon Detector", which identifies Kate as the Paragon of Courage. Elsewhere, Harbinger is secretly contacted by the Anti-Monitor.<ref name="Crisis Part 2 ep">{{Cite episode |title=Crisis on Infinite Earths: Part Two |series=Batwoman |series-link=Batwoman (TV series) |network=[[The CW]] |date=December 9, 2019 |season=1 |number=9}}</ref>

The Paragon detector identifies Barry as the Paragon of Love, [[J'onn J'onzz (Arrowverse)|J'onn J'onzz]] as the Paragon of Honor, and [[Ivy Town (Arrowverse)|Ivy Town]] scientist [[Ryan Choi (Arrowverse)|Ryan Choi]] as the Paragon of Humanity; Iris, Ray, and [[Ralph Dibny (Arrowverse)|Ralph Dibny]] leave to recruit Choi. After the Monitor restores [[Cisco Ramon (Arrowverse)|Cisco Ramon]]'s powers, he, Barry, and [[Caitlin Snow (Arrowverse)|Caitlin Snow]] meet Pariah in the Anti-Monitor's chamber and find an anti-matter cannon powered by [[Earth-90 (Arrowverse)|Earth-90]]'s [[Barry Allen (Arrowverse Earth-90)|Flash]]. When Cisco frees Barry-90, the cannon goes critical, so Pariah recruits Jefferson from his recently destroyed Earth to contain its energy. Barry-1 volunteers to destroy it, but Barry-90 stops him, saying that the Monitor did not specify which Flash would die, and sacrifices himself in his place. Meanwhile, Constantine, Mia, and Diggle visit [[Lucifer Morningstar (Arrowverse Earth-666)|Lucifer]] on [[Earth-666 (Arrowverse)|Earth-666]] for help entering [[purgatory]] and retrieving Oliver's soul. Before they can leave, a [[Spectre (DC Comics character)|Spectre]] named [[Jim Corrigan]] appears and beckons Oliver to come with him, forcing Constantine's team to return to the ''Waverider'' without him. Suddenly, the Anti-Monitor sends a brainwashed Harbinger to kill the Monitor so he can absorb his power and finish destroying the multiverse. Before he is killed, Pariah sends the Paragons to the Vanishing Point, where they witness Lex replace Superman-96 with himself using a Book of Destiny page.<ref name="Crisis Part 3 ep">{{Cite episode |title=Crisis on Infinite Earths: Part Three |series=The Flash |series-link=The Flash (2014 TV series) |network=[[The CW]] |date=December 10, 2019 |season=6 |number=9}}</ref>

On the planet Maltus 10,000 years earlier, Mar Novu attempts to see the birth of the universe, only to end up in the antimatter universe and reveal the multiverse's existence to the Anti-Monitor. Back in the present, following the multiverse's destruction, the Paragons struggle to survive at the Vanishing Point. Once Corrigan teaches him to how use the Spectre's power, Oliver goes to the Vanishing Point to rescue the Paragons and strengthen Barry. Barry drops off Kara, Choi, and Lex on Maltus, but temporarily loses everyone else in the Speed Force after an encounter with the Anti-Monitor. Kara and Choi convince Novu not to implement his plans before Barry takes them and the other Paragons to the dawn of time. There, they learn that the Anti-Monitor will always learn about the multiverse's existence because they only stopped one version of Novu. The Paragons battle the Anti-Monitor and his Shadow Demons until Oliver uses the Spectre's power to restore the multiverse while the Paragons provide help via Lex's page. Despite succeeding, Oliver dies once more, with Barry and Sara at his side.<ref name="Crisis Part 4 ep">{{Cite episode |title=Crisis on Infinite Earths: Part Four |series=Arrow |series-link=Arrow (TV series) |network=[[The CW]] |date=January 14, 2020 |season=8 |number=8}}</ref>

In the recreated universe, the Paragons discover only they remember the crisis and that Earth-1, Earth-38, and Jefferson's Earth were merged into [[Earth-Prime (Arrowverse)|Earth-Prime]], and the multiverse is reborn. J'onn uses his [[psionic]] powers to restore their allies' memories while Sara tries to find Oliver. When the Paragons are attacked by Shadow Demons, a restored Nash discovers that the Anti-Monitor is still alive and plans to resume destroying the multiverse. The heroes find the Anti-Monitor and engage him in battle, buying time for Nash, Ray, Barry, and Choi to develop a bomb that shrinks the Anti-Monitor, banishing him to the microverse. Barry, Kara, Sara, Kate, Clark, J'onn, and Jefferson hold a memorial service for Oliver and agree to protect their new world in his memory.<ref name="Crisis Part 5 ep">{{Cite episode |title=Crisis on Infinite Earths: Part Five |series=Legends of Tomorrow |series-link=Legends of Tomorrow |network=[[The CW]] |date=January 14, 2020 |season=5 |number=1}}</ref>

